  {
   "@id": "https://doi.org/10.82153/pff0-ck46#quote-c9",
   "@type": "Item",
   "format": "text/plain",
   "content": "reframes the experimental data deposited in the PDB as a source of ensemble information",
   "isContainedBy": "https://doi.org/10.82153/pff0-ck46",
   "title": "Wankowicz 2026, Purpose"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:q4",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Can experimental structural data supply the ensemble training data that ensemble predictors lack?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Ensemble predictors need many examples of weighted conformational states. The paper asks whether X-ray and cryo-EM data already in the PDB can provide them."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Purpose; Background, paragraphs 2-3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-026-03084-z"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:q1",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Can heterogeneity hidden in deposited PDB data be recovered automatically across the PDB?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Manual multiconformer modeling in Coot is slow and hard to scale. The paper tests whether qFit can do it for tens of thousands of structures."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Background, paragraphs 4-6",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444904019158",
    "https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004507",
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.4001",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s0907444909030613"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:q2",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Do qFit multiconformer models fit the experimental data better than the deposited models?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Fit is measured by Rfree, compared between each qFit model and the matching re-refined PDB-REDO model."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Results: 'Multiconformer models improve fit to experimental data'"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:q3",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - How much more conformational heterogeneity do qFit models contain than deposited models?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Measured per residue as the change in the number of alternate conformations (altlocs) and in RMSF."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Results: 'Multiconformer models have significantly more conformational heterogeneity compared to static structures'"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c1",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Ensemble prediction is held back by scarce training data",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Current ensemble predictors are trained and benchmarked on molecular dynamics data. Simulations are limited by force field accuracy, accessible timescales and the diversity of systems simulated."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Purpose; Background, paragraph 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.06.14.659707",
    "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.adv9817",
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sbi.2026.103251",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2402.04845",
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuron.2018.08.011",
    "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1800690115",
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/prot.26409"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c8",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Crystallographic data capture heterogeneity regardless of timescale, unlike finite MD trajectories",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "MD gives time-ordered trajectories but undersamples microsecond to millisecond motions; ATLAS, for example, has three 100 ns trajectories per protein. X-ray data report the equilibrium distribution in the crystal but carry no time information and are biased by the crystal environment."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Related datasets of conformational heterogeneity, paragraph 3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkad1084",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06522"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c7",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The qFit dataset is the largest set of experimentally derived multiconformer protein models to date",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "It covers broad sequence and structural diversity and adds experimental ensemble data to training resources that are mostly MD-derived (ATLAS, mdCATH, MISATO, GPCRmd, IDRome)."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Purpose; Related datasets of conformational heterogeneity, paragraph 2; Impact, paragraph 1",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkad1084",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-024-04140-z",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-024-00627-2",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-020-0884-y",
    "https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.5172"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c9",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The PDB's deposited experimental data are a source of ensemble information",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "In most cases the experimental data are too rich to be described by one conformation. Releasing multiconformer models at scale lowers the barrier to using dynamics in routine structural analysis."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Purpose; Impact, paragraph 3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/pff0-ck46#quote-c9"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c11",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Training on single-conformer models may teach predictors local geometric distortions",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Modeling a multi-state residue as one conformer introduces strain. The author proposes, as a possibility, that ensemble training data could help with these artifacts and with the 'last angstrom' gap in side-chain and bond geometry."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Impact, paragraph 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07487-w",
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.06.14.659707",
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.10.10.615955",
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.01.08.631967",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-022-01760-4",
    "https://doi.org/10.7554/elife.90606",
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.06.30.662466"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c2",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Conventional refinement collapses ensemble-averaged data into one structure, so most PDB entries leave heterogeneity unmodeled",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "X-ray and cryo-EM average over many molecules in space and time, but most depositions report a single set of coordinates. Where altlocs are deposited, modeling is uneven across the protein."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Background, paragraph 3; Related datasets of conformational heterogeneity, paragraph 1",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1218231",
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.str.2021.04.010",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/nsmb0306-184",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-022-01760-4",
    "https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkv1316",
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.12.14.628518"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c3",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - qFit can build multiconformer models automatically across tens of thousands of PDB structures",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Starting from PDB-REDO structures at 2 Å or better with structure factors, the pipeline re-refined each model, ran qFit and refined again without manual steps."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Data Generation; Dataset Description"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c10",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - The dataset is limited to high-resolution crystal data and mostly captures side-chain motion",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Only structures better than 2 Å with structure factors are included. Most carry crystal packing and cryogenic constraints, and the heterogeneity found is mostly in side chains rather than the backbone."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Impact, paragraph 4",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2024.01.003"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c4",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - qFit models fit the experimental data better than re-refined deposited models for most structures",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The average Rfree gain is small but reflects modeled heterogeneity. Poor solvent fitting around heterogeneous models partly hides the improvement."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Results: 'Multiconformer models improve fit to experimental data', Figure 3",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/2me0-hd96"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c5",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - qFit models contain widespread side-chain heterogeneity absent from deposited models",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "qFit adds alternate conformations to a minority of residues across the dataset, with the largest spread in long side chains."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Purpose; Results: 'Multiconformer models have significantly more conformational heterogeneity...', Figure 4"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:c6",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Structures with typical, good refinement statistics can still hide unmodeled heterogeneity",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "A deposited model with median-like resolution and R values and no altlocs can still have density that supports multiple conformations."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Results: 'Hidden heterogeneity in a high-quality structure', Figure 5"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:e4",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - 16,133 sequence clusters at 30% identity and 6,590 Foldseek structural clusters",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "MMseqs2 gave 16,133 clusters at 30% sequence identity (many singletons) and 25,608 at 90%. Foldseek gave 6,590 structural clusters."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Dataset Description, paragraph 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/nbt.3988",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41587-023-01773-0"
   ],
   "sourceDocument": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/pff0-ck46"
   ],
   "observationOriginActivity": "qfs:s2"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:e3",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - Re-refined deposited models have a median Rfree of 0.198",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Median Rfree 0.198 (range 0.06 to 0.71) and median Rwork 0.17 (range 0.06 to 0.68). Rfree rises modestly with worse resolution (slope 0.062, R² = 0.22). The roughly 20% residual partly reflects reducing ensemble-averaged data to one discrete model."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Dataset Description, paragraph 1, Figure 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2024.01.003",
    "https://doi.org/10.1111/febs.12922"
   ],
   "observationBase": [
    "https://thestacks-01.s3.amazonaws.com/publications/qfit-at-scale/media_f494fc13_f3b4690c8a1c"
   ],
   "sourceDocument": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/pff0-ck46"
   ],
   "observationOriginActivity": "qfs:s1"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:e1",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - 60,549 of 79,833 structures produced completed qFit models",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "80,876 PDB-REDO structures at 2 Å or better were downloaded; 1,043 nucleic-acid-only structures were removed. Of the 79,833 that entered the pipeline, 60,549 (reported as 85.9%) completed."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Data Generation; Dataset Description, paragraph 1",
   "observationBase": [
    "https://thestacks-01.s3.amazonaws.com/publications/qfit-at-scale/media_48b74625_f3b4690c8a1c"
   ],
   "sourceDocument": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/pff0-ck46"
   ],
   "observationOriginActivity": "qfs:s1"
  },
  {
   "@id": "qfs:e2",
   "@type": [
    "qfs:schema-Evidence",
    "mira:Evidence"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "EVD - Completed models have a median resolution of 1.70 Å and a median of 298 residues",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Resolution ranges from 0.5 to 2.0 Å, residue count from 3 to 2,338, and chain count from 1 to 36."
   },
   "creator": "qfs:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Wankowicz 2026, doi:10.82153/pff0-ck46. Dataset Description, paragraph 1, Figure 1A-C",
   "observationBase": [
    "https://thestacks-01.s3.amazonaws.com/publications/qfit-at-scale/media_48b74625_f3b4690c8a1c"
   ],
